name: diagnostics
kind: inferred
shape: categorical
face: in
membrane: false
note: |
  Fires when a refusal's text or hint changes what it teaches — a
  diagnostic that named the operation now performs it, a message that
  asserted now enumerates. The friction corpus (friction/, mined from
  session journals) is the field instrument: teach-miss rate is how
  often the follow-up to a refusal was a guess or a wrong model, and a
  high-miss family is a message that doesn't teach.

  Witnessed 2026-10-23: KORU021's chain-choke dead-claim (363 corpus
  rows, 28 teach-misses) said "check the spelling against the stages it
  should catch" — the hint named the operation without performing it.
  It now renders the declared alphabet from the same stage_infos the
  check iterates; 210_198's EXPECT pins the enumeration.
route: surface
